I've examined `src/libs/PolicyUtils.ts`. The `isPolicyAdmin` function is defined as:

```javascript
const isPolicyAdmin = (policy: OnyxInputOrEntry<Policy>, currentUserLogin?: string): boolean => getPolicyRole(policy, currentUserLogin) === CONST.POLICY.ROLE.ADMIN;
```

This function checks if the user's role is "admin". The role is determined by `getPolicyRole`:

```javascript
function getPolicyRole(policy: OnyxInputOrEntry<Policy>, currentUserLogin: string | undefined) {
    return policy?.role ?? policy?.employeeList?.[currentUserLogin ?? '-1']?.role;
}
```

This means the user's role can come from either `policy.role` or `policy.employeeList[currentUserLogin].role`. The issue is likely that for a non-admin workspace member, one of these values is incorrectly set to "admin".

Now I will find the localization strings to see what the current empty state messages are. I'll search for `workspace.categories.emptyCategories.title` in the `src/languages` directory.

